# Screens & UX

## Shared UI states (every screen)

Implement explicit components or patterns for:

- **Loading** — skeleton or focused spinner; prefer skeleton for lists/detail
- **Empty** — clear message, optional action
- **Error** — message + retry
- **Content** — the happy path

No blank screens. No infinite spinners without feedback.

---

## Screen 01 — Movie list

- Entry point: upcoming movies from `GET /3/movie/upcoming`
- Must feel **instant** (show cache immediately if available)
- Must hold up as the list grows (virtualization, stable keys, efficient rows)
- Poster + title (+ optional meta: date, rating) — keep rows scannable
- Tap → Movie detail
- Pull-to-refresh when online
- Offline: show last cached list + subtle indicator if stale

---

## Screen 02 — Movie detail

- Data: `GET /3/movie/{id}`, `/videos`, `/images`
- Show core movie info (title, overview, runtime, genres, backdrop/poster as design allows)
- **Trailer:**
  - Available when TMDb returns a playable video (usually YouTube `key`)
  - Opens **full-screen**
  - **Starts automatically**
  - On natural end → **return to detail** without extra user action
  - User can **exit early** at any time → back to detail
  - No dead states (loading player, missing trailer, playback error all handled)
- Construct playback from `site` + `key` (do not expect a ready-made stream URL from TMDb)

---

## Screen 03 — Movie search

- `GET /3/search/movie`
- Must feel **immediate** (debounce input carefully — balance snappiness vs API spam)
- **Freshness rule (non-negotiable):** results on screen must match the **current** query only
  - Ignore or abort responses for older queries
  - Never briefly show results for a query the user has already changed
- Distinguish: idle / typing / loading / no results / error
- Tap result → detail (same detail screen)

---

## Screen 04 — Seat mapping (UI only)

- **No** booking API, **no** persistence, **no** payment, **no** confirmation backend
- Judge: layout, selection states, visual precision, responsiveness
- Typical expectations:
  - Screen / stage indicator
  - Grid or rows of seats
  - States: available, selected, unavailable (and maybe others if designed)
  - Tap to toggle selection where allowed
  - Summary of selected seats (count / labels) is fine as pure UI
  - Works in portrait and landscape without breaking alignment
- Fake static seat map data is acceptable and expected

---

## Visual quality

- Consistent padding and gaps from theme
- Align columns and seat cells deliberately — no “almost” grids
- Typography hierarchy: title vs body vs meta
- Touch targets large enough for mobile
- Landscape: reflow; do not clip primary actions
